distribution, pre-production module created by Espressif
for beta testing purposes; this module used the ESP31B,
the beta testing chip for the ESP32
series.[11][12][13][14][15] FCC Part 15.247 tested (FCC
ID: 2AC7Z-ESP32).[16]
ESP32-WROOM-32 First publicly available ESP32 module board
created by Espressif.[17] FCC Part 15.247 tested (FCC ID:
2AC7Z-ESPWROOM32).[18] Based on ESP32-D0WDQ6 chip.
Originally named "ESP-WROOM-32".
ESP32-WROOM-32E 4,8,16 Same as ESP32-WROOM-32 but with the
Eco V3 processor revisions[19]
ESP32-WROOM-32D 4 Revision of the ESP-WROOM-32 module
which uses an ESP32-D0WD chip instead of an ESP32-D0WDQ6
chip.[20] Originally named "ESP-WROOM-32D".
ESP32-SOLO-1 Similar to the ESP32-WROOM-32D module, but
uses the single-core ESP32-S0WD chip instead of the
dual-core ESP32-D0WD.
